From e772dec667a5bcb1ee04d6765ab3187a6ec18b04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnny Lee <6802342+joseyarashio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:58:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] loop guard: --loop-guard-stop and a per-request
 "loop_guard_stop" end the reply where the guard fires

Port of ashhart/TensorFold af36c7447 (#1463): with the stop policy the stream finishes at the firing token instead
of forcing the think block closed; the reply carries finish_reason "content_filter", tensorfold.loop.stopped and an
error with code "reasoning_loop" (Responses: incomplete/content_filter; Messages: refusal). Default unchanged.

Local addition: a chat request may ask for the policy on itself with "loop_guard_stop": true (passed through the
OpenAI and Responses routes), so a proxy can re-send a looping reply instead of letting the forced close turn into
a read_file call under long context + tools (2026-11-14 A/B: forced close -> 0/7 answers with or without a hint).
